# Changelog

## 0.1.0

The first release with packages to download: Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04, Fedora 44 and
Arch. Kaden is now licensed under the AGPL, version 3 or later.

- **Continuous:** one Kaden with a life of its own beside your chats, behind the switch at
  the top right: their own memory, journal and daily amount, and their own settings
  behind the gear in their view (name, who they are, daily amount, tool settings, saved
  answers).
- **Memory recall:** before the agent answers, the notes from its long-term memory that
  are relevant to what came in are brought before it, as in Claude Code.
- **Claude Code's tools and ways:** its shell, file and web tools, plan mode, subagents
  (also in their own git worktree), AskUserQuestion, hooks and skills.
- **Permissions:** Always allow is one click and names what it keeps; on commands joined
  with `&&`, `;` or `|` it keeps each part, and such a chain runs without asking only when
  every part is allowed. Never allow is under ▾ beside Deny.
- **Notifications:** when Kaden or Continuous waits on your answer and the window is not
  in front, a desktop notification says so.
- **Voice:** talk with Kaden, choose its voice or add one from a recording, and, with an
  NVIDIA GPU, a natural voice; microphone and speaker apart, loaded at start if you like.
- **Watches:** a tool can watch something (new videos, messages) and wake the agent each
  time it happens, also after a restart.
- **A Bilibili account of its own** for the agent, logged in by a QR code you scan: it
  follows channels, hears of their new videos, and reads and sends messages, quickly
  while a conversation is going. Whose messages wake it is a setting.
- **Tool settings:** a Tools module can offer settings, on a Tools page in Settings.
- **Backups** of your chats and Continuous, once a day.
- **Continuous rests and waits sensibly:** it can rest until a time or until something
  wakes it, a check-in says how long it rested, and a question it asks you closes after
  three minutes without an answer, so it never freezes while you are away.
- **macOS:** the file tools, a Seatbelt sandbox for commands and screenshots work on a Mac
  (tested on GitHub's Mac runners); install from source there for now.
- **Sandbox:** on Linux, local sockets under `/run` (Docker, the system bus) are out of a
  sandboxed command's reach. Screenshots use the desktop's screenshot portal.
- **Fixes from a review of the whole codebase,** among them: recall read the right
  project's notes; switching conversations no longer carries a waiting message along;
  clearing every budget limit lasts; Edit keeps a file's CRLF line endings; renaming a
  note onto another's title is refused; a step's arguments read as text.
- Memory stores of earlier builds are not read (one unused column is gone).
- Attachments reach the agent as files, and a look closer to Claude's.

## 0.0.0

First packaged build: the desktop app and the terminal app, with web search, automatic
permissions, a work folder per conversation, long-term memory and tool servers (MCP).
